WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
One dose of medicine, and a
model with invented numbers.

2
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.490
C of t equals twenty e to the
minus nought point three t,

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.020
milligrams per litre,
t hours after the dose.

4
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.750
It starts at twenty and falls fast.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.830
Then it flattens, just above the t axis.

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.450
Wait as long as you like:
the model never gives zero.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.570
Why not?

8
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.400
In this mission, you'll
meet exponential decay,

9
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.830
e to the minus k x, and what
it does at each step in x.

10
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.320
You'll meet horizontal asymptotes, and
use logarithms to find when a model falls

11
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.780
to a given level.

12
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.490
Real doses soon drop below
levels anyone can detect.

13
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.240
The model misses that.

14
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:46.370
Your mission: explain why the model's
concentration never quite reaches zero.
